              "completed": true,
              "summary": "Successfully updated the type annotations for dynamic model callables in `create_react_agent` function in `/home/daytona/langgraph/libs/prebuilt/langgraph/prebuilt/chat_agent_executor.py`. \n\n**Changes made:**\n- Line 255: Changed `Callable[[StateSchema, Runtime[ContextT]], BaseChatModel]` to `Callable[[StateSchema, Runtime[ContextT]], LanguageModelLike]`\n- Line 256: Changed `Callable[[StateSchema, Runtime[ContextT]], Awaitable[BaseChatModel]]` to `Callable[[StateSchema, Runtime[ContextT]], Awaitable[LanguageModelLike]]`\n\n**Impact:**\nThis change widens the accepted return types for dynamic model callables, allowing them to return the result of `bind_tools()` which is `Runnable[LanguageModelInput, BaseMessage]` (aliased as `LanguageModelLike`). This fixes the type annotation bug where dynamic model functions that use `bind_tools()` were incorrectly constrained to return only `BaseChatModel` instead of the broader `LanguageModelLike` type that includes `RunnableBinding` objects returned by `bind_tools()`.\n\nThe change maintains backward compatibility since `BaseChatModel` is a subset of `LanguageModelLike`, while enabling the intended functionality of using models with bound tools in dynamic model callables."
